WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.079
Suppose you are handed two collections of networks,

00:00:03.159 --> 00:00:05.804
each sampled from some unknown distribution,

00:00:05.884 --> 00:00:12.122
and asked a deceptively simple question: were they
generated by the same process or by different ones?

00:00:12.202 --> 00:00:16.457
The nodes carry no shared labels, so you cannot
match them one to one;

00:00:16.537 --> 00:00:19.554
all you can use are the statistics of their edges.

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:22.775
This is the two-sample testing problem for networks,

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:29.340
and it underlies tasks from comparing brain
connectomes to distinguishing biological interaction networks.
